---
/**
 * /learn/japanese-reds/ — third pillar article.
 *
 * Deep-dive on the four most historically important reds in the
 * Japanese tradition: kurenai (safflower crimson), akane (madder),
 * shu (vermilion), and entan (lead red). Each gets cultural context,
 * pigment history, and a working palette recommendation. Heavy
 * internal links to /colors/[slug] pages and /collections/red/.
 */
